 farmers; (k) the amount of agricultural land required to be given up for carbon sequestration and the impact on national food and fibre production; and (l) any other related matters. Sue Lines The question is that business of the Senate No. 2, standing in the name of Senator Hanson, be agreed to.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10696","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-08-19/1"}
